This trick was posted earlier to the net (I didn't invent this myself,
although I did once post how to get multiple copies of an artifact in
pl10 to r.g.h). Anyway **SPOILERS** follow: (Yes this works in pl10.)

The normal limit that a nethack weapon can be enchanted to _with
guaranteed success_ is +8, because any enchantment of a weapon that is
+6 or more has a 33% chance of overevaporating the weapon. (Enchant it
to +5, then read a blessed enchant scroll which will always add +3.)

Normally, nethack only allows you to have one artifact in a given
game, so if you overenchant one, it's gone for the rest of that game.
Obviously, if you had multiple copies of a particular artifact, you
would be able to keep on trying even if you destroyed any particular
one.

Ok, how to get more than one copy of an artifact? The game tries to
have restrictions making sure that the player can't get more than one
copy of any particular one. This is done my "marking" that artifact as
already existing once a player gets a copy. However, suppose a player
could get more than one copy at a particular instant?

The only ways of getting artifacts are finding them, wishing for them,
getting granted them by your god, or making them from ordinary
weapons. The first three methods are already restricted by the
"marking"; however, if a player gets multiple copies of the right
weapon in a single inventory slot, then making the corresponding
artifact will make *all* the copies be that artifact!

There are three weapons one can use this method with to get multiple
copies of: Sting, Orcrist, and Excalibur. To get many Stings, find a
bunch of elven daggers (which tend to always go in the same inventory
slot) and just #name them Sting. Orcrist and Excalibur require Two
handed swords and longswords, which do *not* tend to fall in the same
inventory slot. However, one can get around this by polymorphing a
bunch of darts, arrows, etc, *until* they get a bunch of Two-handed
swords or longswords. Then they can just #name all the Two-handed
swords Orcrist or #dip all the longswords into a fountain and get
multiple copies of these artifacts as well.

Once you have the zillion copies of one of these three artifacts (I
recommand Excalibur since it's by far the best weapon) we can then go
about enchanting it to +20. Let us assume that we #dipped 64 +8
longswords into a fountain and now have 64 blessed +8 rustproof
longswords named Excalibur (in one inventory slot, this is important).
Let's also assume that our blessed enchant weapon scrolls will fail
exactly 1/3 of the time. Now, basically what one does is drop half of
the copies they have in case the ones they are enchanting evaporate.

Drop 32 of the 64 longswords.
Enchant the 32 we are still wielding -> they evaporate.
Pick up the 32 longswords on the ground, and drop 16 of them again.
Enchant the 16 we still have         -> they are now all +11.
Drop 8 of the ones we have on the ground.
Enchant the 8 we still have          -> they are now all +14
Drop 4 of the ones we have on the ground.
Enchant the 4 we still have          -> they evaporate.
Pick of the 4 we have left on the ground, and drop 2 of them again.
Enchant the 2 we still have          -> they are now both +17
Drop one of the ones we have on the ground.
Enchant the one we still have        -> It is now a +20 Excalibur!!!

Note that in the above scenario, we would also still have sixteen +8,
eight +11, two +14, and one +17 Excalibur still on the ground. One
could pick them up and try their luck at still going above +20.

Actually, I would consider this to be the fourth main spoiler as to
how to get a totally kick-butt pl10 nethack character (These should
all get included in the next spoiler file version of course):

1) Ye olde #dip multiple longswords and enchant half of them to get a
   +20 artifact scam.
2) Ye olde polymorph into leprechaun and steal from the temple priest
   to get an AC -128 scam.
3) Ye olde kick the sink and #chat with the succubus to get 1000 hp
   scam.
4) Ye olde polymorph a zillion rocks and carry them to endgame in
   rigged bag of holding to get 50 million points scam.

Combine all four, and you will know why I play Nethack and not Moria ;)

